+{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_VlWuJ54owcamRWw1km90OtDu","content":"1\t# literature-host-interfaces — delta from the plan\n2\t\n3\tWhat the milestone delivered differently from plan r6 as written. Items 1\n4\tto 3 are plan amendments, stated in plan §11 \"close amendments\"; the rest\n5\tare phase-level and recorded in the phase specs' implementation findings.\n6\t\n7\t1. **Retained-file ceiling** (A1). D4's 64 MiB ceiling could never be read\n8\t   back: every JSON reader of the repository refuses over 10 MiB\n9\t   (`gnd.input_policy.MAX_BYTES`). The ceiling is that cap, imported, and\n10\t   the ceiling runs use 9 sections at 1 MiB (LH2 refuted premise).\n11\t2. **Two pull requests** (A2), the reading pair then the admission pair, so\n12\t   that literature-reading-reference's LR3 need not wait for LH4.\n13\t3. **Delegated execution** (A3). The owner's `/process-milestone … auto`\n14\t   superseded D15's phase-by-phase ruling; every spec was approved by\n15\t   delegated ruling.\n16\t4. **LH1 size.** `reading.py` grew by 695 lines and lost 159, past the\n17\t   400-line split threshold; the split was ruled out by delegation (LH1\n18\t   finding 1).\n19\t5. **The retained bound is measured per file** from roster strings, input\n20\t   pins and saved files, not estimated per row (LH1 review r1-F1, r2-F1).\n21\t6. **Handles are keyed as the checker keys them**\n22\t   (`gnd.synth.identity.scalar_identity`): `true` and `1` are two\n23\t   assertions, `1` and `1.0` one (LH3 review r1-F1).\n24\t7. **Rules `reasons`** is a list of value and reason pairs, optional per\n25\t   requirement (LH4 finding 1, review r1-F2).\n26\t8. **The model loads before the judgment route**, so rules are checked\n27\t   first and an edited include refuses `input:model` before the route\n28\t   (LH4 finding 2).\n29\t9. **The `/2` admission record names the shape kind** (`caller` or\n30\t   `packaged`) beside `shape_sha256` (LH4 finding 3).\n31\t10. **Saved receipts are checked at input time** for everything knowable\n32\t    before a call: decision, basis, excerpt digest, digest shape and size\n33\t    (LH1 review r2-F1, r2-F2)."}
+{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_tPKlvH0gyaCHHI10BHP3Gm9i","content":"1\t# literature-host-interfaces — close results\n2\t\n3\tMeasured at the close commit named in `006-milestone-close.md`. Phase\n4\tnumbers are gate outputs quoted in the phase records; the close gates are\n5\tquoted in the close record.\n6\t\n7\t## Goal predicates (plan, \"Goal and completion predicates\")\n8\t\n9\t| Predicate | Result | Evidence |\n10\t|---|---|---|\n11\t| LH1: a public producer protocol; `run()` drives the six stages with a caller's producer over a caller's root; fixture-only steps run on caller data or are recorded skipped; a budget per document; caps as parameters; responses and receipts retained | holds | `002-phase-LH1.md`: LH1-C1 to C14 (T1 to T20, R1 to R9); the three packaged runs equal trees recorded before any edit |\n12\t| LH2: `replay()` re-derives a live run with zero producer and reviewer calls, settings from the run, refusing a changed response, receipt or input | holds | `003-phase-LH2.md`: LH2-C1 to C7 (T1 to T9, R1 to R3) |\n13\t| LH3: admission of a caller-named assertion entity by its own handle; every attached row kept, with the facts of followed entities; optional facts absent; include roots | holds | `004-phase-LH3.md`: LH3-C1 to C10 (T1 to T10, R1 to R5); the packaged call's four H18 digests |\n14\t| LH4: admission rules as caller data, a status of their own, the target cap a parameter | holds | `005-phase-LH4.md`: LH4-C1 to C7 (T1 to T8, R1, R2) |\n15\t| the close cites green focused lanes for LH1 to LH4, the guards, the whole-repository lint | holds at close | `006-milestone-close.md` gates |\n16\t| replies drafted for #216 and #215 | holds | `notes/issue-replies.md` (not posted; the owner posts) |\n17\t| the close review | see the close record | `evidence/close-review/` |\n18\t\n19\t## Review\n20\t\n21\tEach phase diff had one reviewer (Codex, in the other harness, through the\n22\treview helper). Every finding was reproduced, then fixed with a regression\n23\ttest that failed before its fix.\n24\t\n25\t| Phase | Rounds | Findings | Blocking | Last verdict | Unread repair |\n26\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n27\t| LH1 | 2 | 8 | 6 | CHANGES_REQUESTED | `59fd62f0` (round 2 declared last) |\n28\t| LH2 | 1 | 3 | 1 | CHANGES_REQUESTED | `9df661c8` |\n29\t| LH3 | 2 | 5 | 2 | CHANGES_REQUESTED | `f718b572` (round 2 declared last) |\n30\t| LH4 | 1 | 2 | 1 | CHANGES_REQUESTED | `4428a24d` |\n31\t\n32\tThe close panel reads the code at the close commit, every unread repair\n33\tincluded.\n34\t\n35\t## Boundaries\n36\t\n37\t- No live provider ran; producers and reviewers in the tests are local\n38\t  objects. The corpus and provider-budget run stays with the\n39\t  literature-identity follow-up (H20).\n40\t- Time bounds are measured on one machine (Apple silicon).\n41\t- No stable command changed; `gnd judgments check`'s 1,024-target cap stands.\n42\t- The pull requests are open: #241 (reading pair) and #245 (admission pair,\n43\t  stacked on #241). Neither is merged."}
