ompatibility\" |\n588\t| 12 | citations: H10 lines (Claude, GLM), H3 calibration literals (Claude), \"three scenarios\" (GLM) | H10; H3; §2 LH1 \"A caller root\"; R0.2; LH1-C9 |\n589\t\n590\tD14 is recorded as ruled: the owner answered \"full\" when asked which review\n591\tthe plan should get. Fix 2's direction is the owner's: asked how the plan\n592\tshould handle the lint gate, the owner answered \"fix the devtools script\n593\tfirst\", then \"merge pr 34\" and \"override and merge\".\n594\t\n595\t### 2026-11-23, r6: the second round's fixes\n596\t\n597\tAt the owner's request (\"Run round two\") the full panel read r5 and returned\n598\tseven ranked fixes\n599\t([PANEL-REVIEW.md](../../../reviews/literature-host-interfaces-r5-panel/PANEL-REVIEW.md)).\n600\tEvery cited code fact was re-checked at `4ad0d216` before a fix was written,\n601\tand each held. The owner asked for r6 (\"Write r6\"). Every fix is applied;\n602\tsites are tagged `(p2)`.\n603\t\n604\t| Fix | Concern (reviewers) | Sites in r6 |\n605\t|---|---|---|\n606\t| 1 | under D4's defaults the retained-file bound refuses the packaged runs (Claude, blocking); LH1-C14's run at the response and roster ceilings cannot fit the retained-file ceiling (Claude, Codex, Kimi) | §2 LH1 \"Limits\" and \"Retained files\": the bound applies to `/2` runs only, with a derived default cap; D4; LH1-C14; LH2-C3; §6 |\n607\t| 2 | §3 starts LH1 at `4ad0d216`, before the lint re-sync (Claude, Codex, GLM) | completion predicates; §3 start condition |\n608\t| 3 | LH3 keeps every attached row, but LH3-C4 drops one (Codex, blocking) | §2 LH3 \"Attached facts\"; LH3-C4 |\n609\t| 4 | LH1-C10 has no time bound at the route-output and retained-file ceilings (Kimi, GLM) | LH1-C10 |\n610\t| 5 | the frozen two-argument `reading._read` cannot take the recorded cap (Claude) | §2 LH1 \"Retained files\"; §3 LH1 row (`depth.py`); §5 \"Compatibility\" |\n611\t| 6 | which fact type a rule names on the packaged shape (Claude) | §2 LH4 \"The packaged shape\"; LH4-C5 |\n612\t| 7 | `max_rows` on a packaged-shape call bounds nothing (Claude) | §2 LH3 \"Row bound\" and \"Record\"; D18; LH3-C9; LH4-C7 |\n613\t\n614\tNo ruling changed. The plan gate still rules D1–D5, D7, D8, D11–D13, D15, D16\n615\tand D18.\n616\t\n617\t### 2026-11-23, close amendments\n618\t\n619\tRepairs the phase records named, applied at milestone close under the\n620\towner's delegated close ruling (auto=true). Prior wording is r6's.\n621\t\n622\t| Tag | Raised in | Site | Prior wording (r6) | Now |\n623\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n624\t| A1 | `003-phase-LH2.md`, refuted premise and open question Q1 | §10 D4 | \"retained file (…; ceiling 64 MiB). The ceilings cannot all be reached together: at the 1 MiB response ceiling a retained file holds fewer than 64 eligible sections\" | ceiling 10 MiB, `gnd.input_policy.MAX_BYTES`, which every JSON reader of the repository applies, so a larger retained file could never be read back; fewer than 10 eligible sections |\n625\t| A2 | milestone README, \"Deviation from plan §8\" | §8 | \"One pull request from `claude/literature-host-interfaces` to `main`.\" | two pull requests, the reading pair then the admission pair; the milestone-coordinator session relayed the owner's words \"Accept the split\" |\n626\t| A3 | `002-phase-LH1.md`, Gate | §10 D15 | \"The owner selects: phase by phase …\" with the plan gate's phase-by-phase ruling | superseded by the owner's `/process-milestone literature-host-interfaces auto` |\n627\t\n628\tThe other departures from the plan's letter are phase-level and recorded in\n629\tthe phase specs' findings: the LH1 size over the 400-line threshold, the\n630\t`reasons` format of the LH4 rules, and the earlier `input:model` refusal of\n631\tan edited include (close delta)."}
