+{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_9spdHcPc8VHZYpqtDM1ZaLBb","content":"1\t---\n2\tmilestone: literature-host-interfaces\n3\tstation: \"phase-LH3\"\n4\tskill: \"n/a -- repository development, not a gnd-solve station over a domain model\"\n5\tscope: phase-LH3\n6\tdate: 2026-11-23\n7\tgates:\n8\t  - command: \"ruling: delegated (auto=true) approved .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/phase-LH3-spec.md sha256 7de038c63cec4c1cb8a6358e2815947d4ae37cdd0e5c7df1810f1ef56ad72922\"\n9\t    exit: \"n/a -- ruling\"\n10\t  - command: \"uv run pytest -q tests/test_lh3_admission_shape.py tests/test_li4_assertions.py tests/test_li5_lineage.py --tb=short\"\n11\t    exit: 0\n12\t    output: \"68 passed in 46.35s\"\n13\t  - command: \"the project.md structure and inventory guard block (12 files)\"\n14\t    exit: 0\n15\t    output: \"679 passed, 2 deselected in 96.27s (0:01:36)\"\n16\t  - command: \"uv run ruff check\"\n17\t    exit: 0\n18\t    output: \"All checks passed!\"\n19\t  - command: \"python3 scripts/components_index.py changed --base f82490cb --strict\"\n20\t    exit: 0\n21\t    output: \"changed against f82490cb (f82490c): 25 file(s) differ; 0 to fix, 0 warning(s), 0 to reread\"\n22\tslow_cadence:\n23\t  command: \"uv run pytest -q -m \\\"evidence or census\\\"\"\n24\t  trigger: \"explicit owner request or separately scoped CI selection\"\n25\t  reason: \"the broad controls are outside this phase's impact closure\"\n26\tevidence:\n27\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/phase-LH3-spec.md\n28\t    sha256: f5823c57c5fb585c7677f5cb0a110f8ee70e1dc2dfc5770d4cfa706c299cadc4\n29\t  - path: src/gnd/examples/literature/assertion_admission.py\n30\t    sha256: 805535e66257aca50126cf2ea06a44efa99e5fbfe332190149380da7120c9ca4\n31\t  - path: src/gnd/examples/literature/README.md\n32\t    sha256: 2dfd3fcfa1bcae9a17009a55e7b67a4c9b9abc44ef644d55e3e8987e2e567807\n33\t  - path: tests/test_lh3_admission_shape.py\n34\t    sha256: e0573b8e59b79cf6485efb525268df3dde8366e9d39a680f268a28f2f4f65324\n35\t  - path: tests/fixtures/lh3-admission/claims.orm.json\n36\t    sha256: 1518e043a6cb9ae8e5ccac823ca14c8988f04116e2e1153c7888e86811887e15\n37\t  - path: tests/fixtures/lh3-admission/terms.orm.json\n38\t    sha256: 05996ed42c345362ba99884466a7872bbfc11152f7290948c801c87e7dde3370\n39\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/reviews/phase-LH3-r1/review.md\n40\t    sha256: aab6cc702b70aff9b4276bfc664ccb41add101465ddddd585dea4bf94b268662\n41\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/reviews/phase-LH3-r1/FINDINGS.md\n42\t    sha256: cf70e90666253ab1d7a4cc7b61f0eab04d5ba3a261be90f69819a634801e8f05\n43\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/reviews/phase-LH3-r2/review.md\n44\t    sha256: 2573fdbbc32b6b159439c6a92de82c34738191727ce0381592aa98e8f7b7b958\n45\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/reviews/phase-LH3-r2/FINDINGS.md\n46\t    sha256: 2173c132d95e41ad885f7e4bd71899c59298baca18dc62419532002532bb5cb1\n47\t  - path: dev/components/COMPONENTS.md\n48\t    sha256: 60995a6849e00449cfe040e88b03ebb4fef01938ae11039ff1bfe3eae69596c4\n49\t---\n50\t\n51\t# Phase LH3: admission over a caller-named assertion entity\n52\t\n53\t## Claim\n54\t\n55\t`admit(..., shape=SHAPE)` admits the instances of a caller-named entity\n56\ttype, identified by their own handle, with every attached row and the rows\n57\tof followed entities, and writes `literature-assertion-admission/2`. The\n58\tpackaged call keeps its four H18 digests. Criteria and tests in\n59\t`tests/test_lh3_admission_shape.py`:\n60\t\n61\t| Criterion | Tests |\n62\t|---|---|\n63\t| LH3-C1 | T1 (shared passage, two actors and no object, three conditions, a quantity with its rows; `gnd check` on the admitted population exits 0), T1 covers |\n64\t| LH3-C2 | T2 (the packaged `assertion` refuses `shape:objectified-assertion`) |\n65\t| LH3-C3 | T3 |\n66\t| LH3-C4 | T4 |\n67\t| LH3-C5 | T5 (include root bound; an edited include refuses through the judgment route) |\n68\t| LH3-C6 | T6 (eight shape refusals, a target outside the shape, an include path with `..`, three bad `max_rows`, `max_rows` without a shape), R2, R5 |\n69\t| LH3-C7 | T7, R3 |\n70\t| LH3-C8 | T8 (all four H18 digests and the packaged reasons); `test_li4`, `test_li5` unedited |\n71\t| LH3-C9 | T9 (1,024 claims and 65,536 rows within 60 s; one row over refuses `input:row-cap`) |\n72\t| LH3-C10 | T10 (a shared quantity kept once, the rejected claim's rows not kept, `paper` not followed; an empty follow list follows nothing) |\n73\t\n74\t## Gate\n75\t\n76\tDelegated approval (auto=true), 2026-11-23, under the owner's\n77\t`/process-milestone literature-host-interfaces auto`, of the spec at sha256\n78\t`7de038c6…2922` (commit `fe46095e`), LH3-D1 to LH3-D3 as proposed. The spec\n79\thas since been appended only. The coordinator's GO for LH3 approved nothing.\n80\t\n81\t## Review\n82\t\n83\tOne reviewer is one reviewer: Codex in the other harness, read-only,\n84\tthrough `review_tool.py`.\n85\t\n86\t| Round | Read | Findings | Blocking | Self-inflicted |\n87\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n88\t| r1 | the LH3 diff, base `fe46095e` | 4 | 2 | 0 |\n89\t| r2 | the r1 repair, base `dcd3a61c` | 1 | 0 | 0 |\n90\t\n91\tAll five were reproduced and fixed with regression tests that failed before\n92\ttheir fix. Round 2 was declared the last before it ran; its repair\n93\t(`f718b572`) carries no review opinion.\n94\tBoth retained reviews were sanitized of this machine's paths, as their\n95\theaders say.\n96\t\n97\t## Refactoring review\n98\t\n99\tRefactors EXECUTED, behavior-preserving behind T8 and the unedited\n100\t`test_li4`, `test_li5`: the target half of `_support` became\n101\t`_target_reason`, shared by the packaged and generic projections (R0.4).\n102\tDeferred: none. The packaged projection keeps its own path, as D10\n103\trequires.\n104\t\n105\t## Refuted premises and findings\n106\t\n107\tNone refuted. Spec findings 1 to 5 record the departures from the letter:\n108\tinclude paths read with the model parser, cases built in the test module,\n109\tthe `venue` entity, T9's 60 s bound, and T8's four digests. Review found\n110\tthat handles must be keyed as the checker keys them\n111\t(`gnd.synth.identity.scalar_identity`), not as Python keys.\n112\t\n113\t## Open questions\n114\t\n115\tNone opened by this phase.\n116\t\n117\t## Boundary\n118\t\n119\t- **Rules, `policy-refused` and `max_targets` are LH4's.** A shaped call\n120\t  without rules admits every supported assertion.\n121\t- **Nested includes are not copied.** An include root whose include\n122\t  declares includes refuses through the judgment route.\n123\t- **`instances` is `{}`** in the admitted population (LH3-D3).\n124\t- **No review reads round 2's repair.**\n125\t- **Out of scope.** No command-line flag; no change to `gnd judgments\n126\t  check`."}
+{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_WgSEMRHQUXD2GzYE957QBE8E","content":"1\t---\n2\tmilestone: literature-host-interfaces\n3\tstation: \"phase-LH4\"\n4\tskill: \"n/a -- repository development, not a gnd-solve station over a domain model\"\n5\tscope: phase-LH4\n6\tdate: 2026-11-23\n7\tgates:\n8\t  - command: \"ruling: delegated (auto=true) approved .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/phase-LH4-spec.md sha256 ed5f1be11ea35c1e3a5615d39ac4023c3686a55b1545fd181a734286983f712c\"\n9\t    exit: \"n/a -- ruling\"\n10\t  - command: \"uv run pytest -q tests/test_lh4_admission_rules.py tests/test_lh3_admission_shape.py tests/test_li4_assertions.py tests/test_li5_lineage.py --tb=short\"\n11\t    exit: 0\n12\t    output: \"99 passed in 61.05s (0:01:01)\"\n13\t  - command: \"uv run python tools/run_tutorials.py --group literature\"\n14\t    exit: 0\n15\t    output: \"15 tutorial blocks passed\"\n16\t  - command: \"the project.md structure and inventory guard block (12 files)\"\n17\t    exit: 0\n18\t    output: \"679 passed, 2 deselected in 99.85s (0:01:39)\"\n19\t  - command: \"uv run ruff check\"\n20\t    exit: 0\n21\t    output: \"All checks passed!\"\n22\t  - command: \"python3 scripts/components_index.py changed --base ce8d442a --strict\"\n23\t    exit: 0\n24\t    output: \"changed against ce8d442a (ce8d442): 16 file(s) differ; 0 to fix, 0 warning(s), 0 to reread\"\n25\tslow_cadence:\n26\t  command: \"uv run pytest -q -m \\\"evidence or census\\\"\"\n27\t  trigger: \"explicit owner request or separately scoped CI selection\"\n28\t  reason: \"the broad controls are outside this phase's impact closure\"\n29\tevidence:\n30\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/phase-LH4-spec.md\n31\t    sha256: c78f2578899890ba579db643942724a659ac4eb8455ce528aaedd7a4589d6658\n32\t  - path: src/gnd/examples/literature/assertion_admission.py\n33\t    sha256: bc78375fb84d95f8497e519dce67ca8dd55a376764c0b03ad907b363e37856a6\n34\t  - path: src/gnd/examples/literature/README.md\n35\t    sha256: 518990cc7568ac9949d2f813b7745a829d7c00b58ed8d07835744bc2de9a0d51\n36\t  - path: tests/test_lh4_admission_rules.py\n37\t    sha256: 4df73aaec6962b66d79d099cc5606341451132e5a64ffcea3700edc49d259547\n38\t  - path: tests/test_lh3_admission_shape.py\n39\t    sha256: 8196e84b454028c5cc2fddc5ff13626909e00ccff71642dcb3f2dee4ea80e366\n40\t  - path: docs/literature/commands.md\n41\t    sha256: 26485303f60ba06c426613f1b275468e6bd7b49b7523e5b9665f50b858252cde\n42\t  - path: docs/release-notes.md\n43\t    sha256: 1fa3010f9d0b60380e4933508250d3f984ef235a3b861c48b56488a1fe24f3bd\n44\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/reviews/phase-LH4-r1/review.md\n45\t    sha256: 3333bd3218376dc8827ab362d4b8330d6ac8b2ec138023533b9e3abe313cb6cd\n46\t  - path: .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/reviews/phase-LH4-r1/FINDINGS.md\n47\t    sha256: 70a233ba4a899ec88efbe6fafb00ee39b7a464f9c0131edf3c843b98f0b9d299\n48\t---\n49\t\n50\t# Phase LH4: admission rules as data\n51\t\n52\t## Claim\n53\t\n54\t`admit(..., rules=RULES, max_targets=N)`, with or without a shape, admits\n55\tthe supported assertions that satisfy the rules, records the others as\n56\t`policy-refused` with the first failing requirement's reason, and binds\n57\tevery setting in a `/2` record. The packaged comparison is now\n58\t`DEFAULT_RULES`, run by the one evaluator, and the packaged call keeps its\n59\tbytes. Criteria and tests in `tests/test_lh4_admission_rules.py`:\n60\t\n61\t| Criterion | Tests |\n62\t|---|---|\n63\t| LH4-C1 | T1 (two rules files, two admitted sets: `{c1}` and `{c1, c3}`) |\n64\t| LH4-C2 | T2 |\n65\t| LH4-C3 | T3 (one admissible and one inadmissible row; no row) |\n66\t| LH4-C4 | T4 (a cap below the policy, 1,025, 0, `True`; a cap at the policy size admits) |\n67\t| LH4-C5 | T5 (ten malformed or unknown-name rules documents and the packaged-shape `assertion_names_work` rule, all before the judgment route), R1 |\n68\t| LH4-C6 | T6 (default rules passed explicitly: same reasons, order and admitted bytes, `policy-refused` for statements 3 to 6); LH3's T8 pins the four H18 digests of the call with no argument |\n69\t| LH4-C7 | T7 (each of shape, rules, `max_targets`, `max_rows` changes its field; a rules-only call records `packaged`, `null`, `null`) |\n70\t| rule 2 | T8 (64 requirements over 65,536 rows within 60 s) |\n71\t\n72\t## Gate\n73\t\n74\tDelegated approval (auto=true), 2026-11-23, under the owner's\n75\t`/process-milestone literature-host-interfaces auto`, of the spec at sha256\n76\t`ed5f1be1…712c` (commit `8fffc161`), LH4-D1 and LH4-D2 as proposed. The\n77\tspec has since been appended only. The coordinator's GO for LH4 approved\n78\tnothing.\n79\t\n80\t## Review\n81\t\n82\tOne reviewer is one reviewer: Codex in the other harness, read-only,\n83\tthrough `review_tool.py`, one round over the LH4 diff (base `8fffc161`).\n84\tTwo findings, both reproduced, one blocking and one hardening, none\n85\tself-inflicted; both fixed at `4428a24d` with regression tests that failed\n86\tbefore the fix. The convergence rules did not call for a second round; the\n87\trepairs carry no review opinion. The retained review was sanitized of this\n88\tmachine's paths, as its header says.\n89\t\n90\t## Refactoring review\n91\t\n92\tRefactors EXECUTED, behavior-preserving behind LH3's T8, LH4's T6 and the\n93\tunedited `test_li4`, `test_li5`: the literal comparison of\n94\t`project()` (`(polarity, attribution) != (\"asserts\", \"own-finding\")`) became\n95\t`DEFAULT_RULES` evaluated by `_evaluate_rules`, the one evaluator of both\n96\tprojections (R0.4). Deferred: none.\n97\t\n98\t## Refuted premises and findings\n99\t\n100\tNone refuted. Spec findings 1 to 4: `reasons` is a list of value and reason\n101\tpairs, not a mapping keyed by JSON text; the model loads before the judgment\n102\troute, so an edited include refuses `input:model` (LH3's T5 updated); the\n103\t`/2` record names the shape kind; `_case` gained `edit_model`.\n104\t\n105\t## Open questions\n106\t\n107\tNone opened by this phase.\n108\t\n109\t## Boundary\n110\t\n111\t- **Rules name attached fact types only**, never followed ones.\n112\t- **1,024 targets per call** is `gnd judgments check`'s cap; a larger set is\n113\t  admitted in several calls the host makes (D11).\n114\t- **No review reads `4428a24d`'s repairs.**\n115\t- **Out of scope.** No command-line flag; no change to `gnd judgments\n116\t  check`."}
