+{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_7OAz228Qx0bHczIPGG3FMUeL","content":"1\t---\n2\tmilestone: literature-host-interfaces\n3\tstation: plan-gate\n4\tscope: plan-gate\n5\tdate: 2026-11-23\n6\tskill: \"start-milestone (planning); the gate ruled by the owner, auto=false\"\n7\tgates:\n8\t  - command: \"uv run python tools/run_gnd_review_panel.py review-request.json --out panel-run --reviewer-timeout 600 --overall-timeout 900\"\n9\t    exit: 0\n10\t  - command: \"uv run gnd review finalize panel-run synthesis.json --out PANEL-REVIEW.md\"\n11\t    exit: 0\n12\t  - command: \"uv run python tools/run_gnd_review_panel.py review-request.json --out panel-run --reviewer-timeout 600 --overall-timeout 900\"\n13\t    exit: 0\n14\t  - command: \"uv run gnd review finalize panel-run synthesis.json --out PANEL-REVIEW.md\"\n15\t    exit: 0\n16\t  - command: \"ruling: owner approved .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/literature-host-interfaces-plan.md sha256 2dc760e58dbd1b95396695b1c9690443dc62af91bae52b1c3b4ee0dfa3e01528\"\n17\t    exit: \"n/a -- ruling\"\n18\tevidence:\n19\t  - path: .gnd-planning/reviews/literature-host-interfaces-r4-panel/PANEL-REVIEW.md\n20\t    sha256: 9e761cbc0f7650917f08a17d90b07e7901a06434d2a3e80f700dc27c4ae772ac\n21\t  - path: .gnd-planning/reviews/literature-host-interfaces-r5-panel/PANEL-REVIEW.md\n22\t    sha256: 73e3c873b36f9e8593c28495625889c31c60510b4c2e253443a89d7dd01866f6\n23\t---\n24\t\n25\t# Plan gate: literature-host-interfaces r6\n26\t\n27\tDate: 2026-11-23. `auto=false`.\n28\t\n29\t## Gate output (verbatim)\n30\t\n31\tThe gate is the owner's ruling, given in the planning session on 2026-11-23.\n32\tThe driving agent listed the thirteen open decisions and asked whether to\n33\trule all thirteen as proposed, with D15 phase by phase, or to change some.\n34\tThe owner answered:\n35\t\n36\t> All as proposed\n37\t\n38\tThe full digest of the approved bytes was computed from the working file\n39\tbefore this record was written:\n40\t\n41\t| Artifact | SHA-256 |\n42\t|---|---|\n43\t| `notes/literature-host-interfaces-plan.md` (r6) | `2dc760e58dbd1b95396695b1c9690443dc62af91bae52b1c3b4ee0dfa3e01528` |\n44\t\n45\t**The plan is not edited to record its own approval.** Its status line still\n46\treads \"not approved\", and its §10 rows still read \"Proposed\". This record is\n47\twhat changes that.\n48\t\n49\t## Rulings\n50\t\n51\tFive decisions were ruled before the gate and are tagged `(o)` in the plan:\n52\t\n53\t- D6: as proposed (2026-11-22).\n54\t- D9: the other reading, follow entities outward (2026-11-22).\n55\t- D10: the other reading, own handle only (2026-11-22).\n56\t- D14: the full GND panel (2026-11-23).\n57\t- D17: as proposed (2026-11-23).\n58\t\n59\tThe gate rules the other thirteen as the plan's §10 proposes them:\n60\t\n61\t| Decision | Ruling |\n62\t|---|---|\n63\t| D1 producer protocol home | in `reading.py`, until a second example uses it |\n64\t| D2 LH4 disposition | `policy-refused`, in the `/2` record only; `/1` keeps `fail` |\n65\t| D3 fixture-only steps | calibration, the conflict check and the absence scope are optional and declared in the profile; an undeclared step is `skipped`; the label is profile data; a reviewer is optional, and any decision other than `supported` refuses the run |\n66\t| D4 limits | seven limits with the defaults and ceilings in §10. The retained-file cap of a `/2` run is derived from the run's bounds and is never less than 128 KiB. `document_budget`'s ceiling is the largest-budget limit |\n67\t| D5 reading manifest | `literature-reading-run/2` for any run that uses a new argument; `/1` is unchanged otherwise |\n68\t| D7 malformed response or raising producer | refuse the run with nothing written |\n69\t| D8 judged unit | targets are attached rows; supported means at least one target and every target admitted |\n70\t| D11 `max_targets` ceiling | 1,024, the stable command's cap |\n71\t| D12 admission record | `literature-assertion-admission/2`; the packaged call keeps `/1` |\n72\t| D13 phase diff reviewer | the review helper, subject `phase`, one reviewer in a different tool |\n73\t| D15 how the milestone runs | phase by phase, with an owner gate on each spec (`auto=false`) |\n74\t| D16 caller-run route exits | 0, 1, 2 and 4 are recorded and the run completes; any other exit refuses |\n75\t| D18 generic row bound | `max_rows`, default 16,384, ceiling 65,536; `max_rows` without a shape refuses |\n76\t\n77\tD15's proposal was \"the owner selects\". The owner's \"All as proposed\"\n78\tanswered a question that offered phase by phase as the proposal, so D15 is\n79\trecorded as phase by phase. No delegation (`auto=true`) is given for this\n80\tmilestone.\n81\t\n82\t## Plan review\n83\t\n84\tThe instrument was the full GND review panel (D14). It ran twice, each time\n85\tfrom a disposable clone at `4ad0d216` with the uncommitted planning files\n86\tcopied in. The run records hold the provenance checks, the reviewer outcomes\n87\tand the verified facts.\n88\t\n89\t**Round 1, over r4** (sha256 `6cadaa9134585b348d53ef50ef5c35638a3b0bb20c7c36726ac53039ac357cb6`;\n90\t[record](../../reviews/literature-host-interfaces-r4-panel/README.md)):\n91\t\n92\t- Outcome: four of six reviewers succeeded, all `revise`. Qwen timed out, and Gemini returned malformed output.\n93\t- Findings: two blocking concerns and twelve ranked fixes.\n94\t- Disposition: r5 applied all twelve, tagged `(p1)`. For fix 2 (the lint gate), the owner had the dev-tools scripts fixed upstream (dev-tools PR 34, `a29562a`), and the re-sync is part of this milestone's planning change.\n95\t\n96\t**Round 2, over r5** (sha256 `c1a832378a2f303cdf1be8884ea61e745eca7f22e4fab19a449761d62b082c9b`;\n97\t[record](../../reviews/literature-host-interfaces-r5-panel/README.md)):\n98\t\n99\t- Outcome: five of six reviewers succeeded. Gemini was `approve`; Claude, Codex, Kimi and GLM were `revise`. Qwen timed out.\n100\t- Findings: three agreed concerns, one single-reviewer blocking concern on the retained-file bound, and seven ranked fixes.\n101\t- Disposition: r6 applied all seven, tagged `(p2)`. Plan §11 maps every fix of both rounds to its sites.\n102\t\n103\t**No opinion on r6.** The convergence rules allow two rounds, so no panel read\n104\tr6. Its new sentences carry no review opinion, and this approval adds none.\n105\t\n106\t## What the approval leaves open\n107\t\n108\t- **The LH1 spec is not approved.** The draft\n109\t  `notes/phase-LH1-spec.md` (sha256\n110\t  `b3270ded71564d02d8aa0dc806872a53b02c6a4b3b3272c6538348a31f38e416`) has\n111\t  its own owner gate, including its decisions LH1-D1 to LH1-D5. No code may be\n112\t  written before that gate.\n113\t- **The LH1 start commit.** Plan §3 sets it as the merge that lands this plan\n114\t  with the dev-tools re-sync. That commit does not exist yet, and the LH1 spec\n115\t  records it.\n116\t- **LH2 to LH4** each need their own spec and gate.\n117\t\n118\t## Selection\n119\t\n120\tNo phase has been selected. Execution starts only when the owner explicitly\n121\tselects `process-phase LH1 literature-host-interfaces`.\n122\t\n123\t## Boundary\n124\t\n125\t- **Later phases.** Approving the plan does not approve any phase spec.\n126\t- **Planning record only.** This record authorizes no implementation, push,\n127\t  PR, merge, release or publication.\n128\t- **Uncommitted bytes.** The digests above are of working-tree files. They\n129\t  become citations only once the files are committed together with this\n130\t  record."}
