as read especially: the R1-R9/R1-R3/R1-R5/R1-R2 regression tests and their fixes (measured retained bounds, unserializable answers and receipts, saved-receipt validation before any producer call, supersession-source stop fix, non-UTF-8 sources, boolean-vs-number handles, opaque values, scalar rule values) are all present and coherent; the retained-cap arithmetic is measured from actual canonical bytes and covers every retained file including stage records, payloads, receipts and coverage rows.\"}\n{\"concern_id\":\"close-record-evidence-missing\",\"evidence\":[{\"artifact_path\":\".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/close-results.md\",\"location\":\"lines 15-17\",\"observation\":\"close-results.md asserts two goal-predicate rows with evidence pointers that do not resolve at this commit: \\\"| the close cites green focused lanes for LH1 to LH4, the guards, the whole-repository lint | holds at close | `006-milestone-close.md` gates |\\\" and \\\"| the close review | see the close record | `evidence/close-review/` |\\\". Neither .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/006-milestone-close.md nor .gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/evidence/close-review/ exists in the tree (the directory holds only 001-plan-gate.md, 002-005 phase records, README.md and notes/). The plan's own completion predicate requires them: literature-host-interfaces-plan.md lines 66-69, \\\"The milestone is closed when each phase has its record and the close record cites green focused lanes for LH1-LH4, the structure and inventory guards, the whole-repository `uv run ruff check`, as `project.md` requires `(p1)`, the replies drafted for #216 and #215, and the close review.\\\"\"}],\"recommendation\":\"Write 006-milestone-close.md with the close gates and populate evidence/close-review/ (or retarget the citations), so the two asserted predicates are supported by records at the close commit; until then the milestone is not demonstrably closed.\",\"relevance\":\"blocking\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"title\":\"Close-results cites a close record and close-review evidence that do not exist at this commit\"}\n{\"concern_id\":\"delta-omits-lane-departure\",\"evidence\":[{\"artifact_path\":\".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/close-delta.md\",\"location\":\"line 5\",\"observation\":\"close-delta.md states \\\"Items 1 to 3 are plan amendments...; the rest are phase-level and recorded in the phase specs' implementation findings\\\", and items 4-10 list the phase-level departures. One plan-level departure is missing from it: plan §9 (literature-host-interfaces-plan.md lines 491-496) fixes the focused lanes as e.g. \\\"uv run pytest -q tests/test_lh1_reading_host.py tests/test_ld3_reading_workflow.py ...\\\", but every phase record's gate actually ran with tests/test_ld1_competency_examples.py appended (002-phase-LH1.md gate note: \\\"plan §9 LH1 row plus tests/test_ld1_competency_examples.py, added because depth.py changed (spec finding 9)\\\"; the same addition appears in 003, and the LH3/LH4 lanes analogously). This departure is recorded in the phase records but not in the delta that claims to list what the milestone delivered differently from plan r6.\"}],\"recommendation\":\"Add an eleventh delta item noting the focused-lane addition of tests/test_ld1_competency_examples.py (LH1 spec finding 9), or state explicitly that gate-lane changes are out of the delta's scope.\",\"relevance\":\"completeness\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"title\":\"Delta omits the focused-lane departure recorded only in the phase gate notes\"}"}
