+{"concern_id":"status-block-contradicts-d15-a3","evidence":[{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/literature-host-interfaces-plan.md","location":"status block, second and fourth paragraphs; §8 second bullet; §10 D15","observation":"The file opens '**Status: r6 draft, 2026-11-23. Not approved; r6's own bytes are not reviewed.**' and states 'No plan-gate record exists. The owner gates the plan before any spec is approved and before any code.', with §8 promising 'The plan gate is recorded in `001-plan-gate.md` once the owner rules, with the review's instrument, reviewed digest and dispositions, or the statement that none ran.' The same bytes then record in D15: 'Ruled at the plan gate as phase by phase; superseded on 2026-11-23 by the owner's `/process-milestone literature-host-interfaces auto` (close A3)'. The close amendments touched §10 and §8 but not the status block."},{"artifact_path":".gnd-planning/milestones/literature-host-interfaces/notes/close-delta.md","location":"item 3","observation":"'**Delegated execution** (A3). The owner's `/process-milestone … auto` superseded D15's phase-by-phase ruling; every spec was approved by delegated ruling.' The delta therefore describes a gated, approved and fully executed plan whose own header still says it is an unapproved draft with no gate record."}],"recommendation":"Update the status block (or add an A4 row) to say that the gate ruled, that r6 with A1 to A3 is the approved spec, and where the gate ruling is recorded — including plainly whether 001-plan-gate.md was ever written — so the spec's header does not contradict D15, A3 and the close delta.","relevance":"completeness","severity":"low","title":"The spec's status block still declares the plan unapproved and ungated, contradicting D15 and A3 in the same bytes"}
