ssing from it: plan §9 (literature-host-interfaces-plan.md lines 491-496) fixes the focused lanes as e.g. \"uv run pytest -q tests/test_lh1_reading_host.py tests/test_ld3_reading_workflow.py ...\", but every phase record's gate actually ran with tests/test_ld1_competency_examples.py appended (002-phase-LH1.md gate note: \"plan §9 LH1 row plus tests/test_ld1_competency_examples.py, added because depth.py changed (spec finding 9)\"; the same addition appears in 003, and the LH3/LH4 lanes analogously). This departure is recorded in the phase records but not in the delta that claims to list what the milestone delivered differently from plan r6."}],"recommendation":"Add an eleventh delta item noting the focused-lane addition of tests/test_ld1_competency_examples.py (LH1 spec finding 9), or state explicitly that gate-lane changes are out of the delta's scope.","relevance":"completeness","severity":"low","title":"Delta omits the focused-lane departure recorded only in the phase gate notes"}],"disposition":"revise","reviewer_id":"kimi","schema_version":2,"summary":"Checked the goal predicates and criteria LH1-C1..LH4-C7 against src/gnd/examples/literature/reading.py, depth.py, assurance_report.py, assertion_admission.py and the four test files at the close commit; the delivered code and tests substantively meet the criteria, all ten close-delta items are true of the code and justified, and the four unread repairs (59fd62f0, 9df661c8, f718b572, 4428a24d) are present in the recorded bytes with their regression tests. Two concerns: the close-results table asserts completion predicates whose cited evidence (006-milestone-close.md and evidence/close-review/) does not exist at this commit, and the delta omits one small recorded departure. What I verified: A1 (retained ceiling is gnd.input_policy.MAX_BYTES = 10 MiB, imported as LIMIT_CEILINGS['retained_bytes'] at reading.py:70 and tested by test_lh1 R9); A2/A3 (README deviation and phase delegated rulings); delta items 4-10 (measured per-file retained bound in _retained_cap reading.py:915-960; scalar_identity handle keying assertion_admission.py:21,296-300; reasons-as-pairs 144-158; model-before-route 500-510; shape kind in the /2 record 527-531; input-time receipt checks reading.py:362-378). The unread-repair code was read especially: the R1-R9/R1-R3/R1-R5/R1-R2 regression tests and their fixes (measured retained bounds, unserializable answers and receipts, saved-receipt validation before any producer call, supersession-source stop fix, non-UTF-8 sources, boolean-vs-number handles, opaque values, scalar rule values) are all present and coherent; the retained-cap arithmetic is measured from actual canonical bytes and covers every retained file including stage records, payloads, receipts and coverage rows."},"response_salvage":{"complete":false,"declared_concern_count":2,"dropped":[],"dropped_overflow":0,"preamble_lines":1,"retained_concern_count":2,"trailing_lines":0,"transport":"jsonl"},"reviewer_id":"kimi","schema_version":1,"status":"success"},{"capability":{"argv_count":2,"argv_sha256":"e7d7ebabc51f1132a879fd95119b7394fb117047398e6d61bd92032ce4b15e67","elapsed_seconds":0.28258291725069284,"ended_monotonic":4076877.188927708,"environment":[{"name":"ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"HOME","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"LOGNAME","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"NO_COLOR","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"OPENROUTER_API_KEY","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"PATH","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"PYTHONUNBUFFERED","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"TMPDIR","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"USER","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"ZAI_API_KEY","provenance":"supplied"}],"process_group_cleaned":true,"return_code":0,"signal":null,"spawn_error":null,"spawned":true,"started_monotonic":4076876.906344791,"status":"succeeded","stderr":{"observed_bytes":0,"path":"reviewers/glm/capability.stderr","retained_bytes":0,"sha256":