erage rows with their eight states are unchanged” and defines producer outcomes as “accepted”, “empty”, and “refused”. In src/gnd/examples/literature/reading.py:504–507, an `accepted` answer with `facts={\"paper_title\":[]}` passes because the mapping is nonempty and `_fact_rows` permits an empty row list. At reading.py:611–614, the presence of the `paper_title` key makes its question `supported` despite there being no fact row. Caller check exits 0, 1, 2, and 4 are allowed at reading.py:689–700, so an inadequate population need not stop the run. tests/test_lh1_reading_host.py:297–299 checks `accepted` with an empty mapping and `empty` with an empty row list, but omits this combination."}],"recommendation":"Derive `supported` from a nonempty fact row list, and either refuse an `accepted` response with no rows or define its coverage outcome explicitly. Add the empty-list case to the producer tests.","relevance":"blocking","severity":"high","title":"An empty fact list is reported as supported coverage"}],"disposition":"revise","reviewer_id":"codex","schema_version":2,"summary":"A caller run can report a question as supported when its producer supplied no fact rows."},"response_salvage":{"complete":true,"declared_concern_count":1,"dropped":[],"dropped_overflow":0,"preamble_lines":0,"retained_concern_count":1,"trailing_lines":0,"transport":"jsonl"},"reviewer_id":"codex","schema_version":1,"status":"success"},{"capability":{"argv_count":2,"argv_sha256":"1b5bc357d2bd4be5d1bbff5efaac005984be935cdbc9a265cc82ae5e71949319","elapsed_seconds":0.1403485001064837,"ended_monotonic":4076877.025487,"environment":[{"name":"HOME","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"LOGNAME","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"NO_COLOR","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"OPENAI_API_KEY","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"OPENROUTER_API_KEY","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"PATH","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"PYTHONUNBUFFERED","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"TMPDIR","provenance":"supplied"},{"name":"US